            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0210" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/512.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé MacMurray.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of the
                    Legation’s despatch No. 299 of July 8, 1914, enclosing report of Mr. C. L. L.
                    Williams on the status of the claims arising out of the revolution of 1911.</p>
                <p>The Department regards Mr. Williams as deserving of commendation for his
                    excellent work as claims delegate.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
